 style=\"border: 8px solid #f9c74f; padding: 15px; background-color: #ffffff; line-height:25px\"> \n","    \n","### **Bitcoin Data at a Glance**\n","\n","Bitcoin (BTC-USD) is the world's first and most valuable cryptocurrency, often seen as \"digital gold\" due to its finite supply and decentralized nature. Since its inception in 2009, Bitcoin has transformed from a niche innovation to a global financial asset, attracting attention from institutional investors, traders, and everyday users alike. Its price is highly volatile and driven by a complex interplay of supply and demand, market sentiment, macroeconomic trends, and technological developments.\n","\n","The Bitcoin Price dataset provides historical market data sourced from Yahoo Finance, covering a wide date range from January 1, 2015, to January 1, 2025. This dataset captures detailed information about Bitcoin’s daily performance, allowing for comprehensive analysis and modeling of its price movements.\n","\n","\n","- **Open**-The price of Bitcoin at the beginning of the trading day\n","    \n","- **High**-The highest price reached by Bitcoin during the day\n","    \n","- **Low**-The lowest price recorded during the trading day\n","    \n","- **Close**-The final price of Bitcoin at the close of the trading day\n","    \n","- **Adj Close**-The closing price adjusted for splits and dividends (not relevant for crypto, but included by Yahoo)\n","    \n","- **Volume**-The total trading volume of Bitcoin in USD across exchanges on that day\n","\n","This dataset is an excellent resource for anyone seeking to understand the dynamics of Bitcoin’s market behavior. It enables users to identify long-term trends, capture short-term price fluctuations, and evaluate the impact of macroeconomic and crypto-specific events on Bitcoin prices. The data can be utilized for various types of analysis such as exploratory data analysis (EDA), time series forecasting, and predictive modeling using techniques like ARIMA, LSTM, and Transformer-based models. Additionally, visual tools such as candlestick charts, moving averages, and volatility plots can help provide deeper insight into Bitcoin’s unique market patterns."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"621035a6","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2025-10-21T10:42:55.266529Z","iopub.status.busy":"2025-10-21T10:42:55.266168Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-10-21T10:44:55.506699Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-10-21T10:44:55.505694Z"},"papermill":{"duration":120.261444,"end_time":"2025-10-21T10:44:55.509147","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-10-21T10:42:55.247703","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Collecting torchviz\r\n","  Downloading torchviz-0.0.3-py3-none-any.whl.metadata (2.1 kB)\r\n","Requirement already satisfied: torch in /usr/local/lib/python3.11/dist-packages (from torchviz) (2.6.0+cu124)\r\n","Requirement already satisfied: graphviz in /usr/local/lib/python3.11/dist-packages (from torchviz) (0.21)\r\n","Requirement already satisfied: filelock in /usr/local/lib/python3.11/dist-packages (from torch->torchviz) (3.18.0)\r\n","Requirement already satisfied: typing-extensions>=4.10.0 in /usr/local/lib/python3.11/dist-packages (from torch->torchviz) (4.14.0)\r\n","Requirement already satisfied: networkx in /usr/local/lib/python3.11/dist-packages (from torch->torchviz) (3.5)\r\n","Requirement already satisfied: jinja2 in /usr/local/lib/python3.11/dist-packages (from torch->torchviz) (3.1.6)\r\n","Requirement already satisfied: fsspec in /usr/local/lib/python3.11/dist-packages (from torch->torchviz) (2025.5.1)\r\n","Collecting nvidia-cuda-nvrtc-cu12==12.4.127 (from torch->torchviz)\r\n","  Downloading nvidia_cuda_nvrtc_cu12-12.4.127-py3-none-manylinux2014_x86_64.whl.metadata (1.5 kB)\r\n","Collecting nvidia-cuda-runtime-cu12==12.4.127 (from torch->torchviz)\r\n","  Downloading nvidia_cuda_runtime_cu12-12.4.127-py3-none-manylinux2014_x86_64.whl.metadata (1.5 kB)\r\n","