"},"tags":[]},"source":["<a id=\"an\"></a>\n","\n","<h1 style=\"\n","    background-color:#264653; \n","    background-size: cover;\n","    background-position: center;\n","    font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\n","    font-size: 1.5em;\n","    color: white;\n","    text-align: center;\n","    padding: 15px;\n","    border-radius: 15px 50px;\n","    border: 1px solid black;\n","\">\n","    Analysis of Technical Indicators\n","</h1>"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"f3c791b0","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.132983,"end_time":"2025-10-21T10:45:43.068749","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-10-21T10:45:42.935766","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["<a id=\"ann\"></a>\n","\n","<h1 style=\" \n","    background-color:#cddcdf; \n","    background-position: center;\n","    font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\n","    font-size: 1.5em;\n","    color: Black;\n","    text-align: center;\n","    padding: 15px;\n","    border-radius: 5px 10px;\n","\">\n","    Daily Price Change Analysis\n","</h1>"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"d7695c30","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.129715,"end_time":"2025-10-21T10:45:43.329675","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-10-21T10:45:43.19996","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["<div style=\"border: 2px solid #264653; padding: 15px; background-color: #ffffff;line-height:25px\">\n","    \n","**Daily Return Percentage of Bitcoin** measures the day-to-day percentage change in Bitcoin’s price. It is calculated by comparing the closing price of a given day with that of the previous day, showing how much the price has increased or decreased in percentage terms. This metric is essential for understanding Bitcoin’s volatility and short-term price movements, providing valuable insight into market momentum and risk.\n","\n","Mathematically, it is expressed as:\n","\n","$$\n","\\text{Daily Return \\%} = \\left(\\frac{\\text{Close}_t - \\text{Close}_{t-1}}{\\text{Close}_{t-1}}\\right) \\times 100\n","$$\n","\n","Where:\n","\n","* $\\text{Close}_t$ is the closing price on day $t$,\n","* $\\text{Close}_{t-1}$ is the closing price on the previous day.\n","\n","**Volatility** refers to the degree of variation or fluctuation in Bitcoin’s price over time. High volatility indicates that Bitcoin’s price changes rapidly and unpredictably, experiencing large swings both upward and downward. Conversely, low volatility means the price is relatively stable and changes more gradually. Volatility is commonly measured by the standard deviation of daily returns over a specific time window and is a crucial metric for assessing the risk and potential reward of trading or investing in Bitcoin.\n","\n","Analyzing daily returns along with volatility helps investors and traders better gauge market sentiment and make informed decisions regarding entry and exit points."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":25,"id":"7f7f9639","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2025-10-21T10:45:43.594986Z","iopub.status.busy":"2025-10-21T10:45:43.594702Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-10-21T10:45:44.395014Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-10-21T10:45:44.394052Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.938459,"end_time":"2025-10-21T10:45:44.399849","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-10-21T10:45:43.46139","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 2200x1600 with 4 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n","\n","# Calculate daily return percentage\n","df['Daily_Return'] = df['Close'].pct_change() * 100  # in percent\n","\n","# Calculate rolling volatility (standard deviation) over 30 days\n","df['Rolling_Volatility'] = df['Daily_Return'].rolling(window=30).std()\n","\n","# Get summary statistics for Daily_Return\n","stats = df['Daily_Return'].describe()\n","\n","# Make the figure wider and taller overall\n","fig = plt.figure(figsize=(22, 16))  # wider and taller\n","\n","# Grid spec: 2 rows, 3 columns\n","# Increase height of first row for bigger daily return plot (like 18x14)\n","# Second row smaller height (like 18x10)\n","gs = fig.add_gridspec(2, 3, width_ratios=[1, 1, 0.5], height_ratios=[3, 2], wspace=0.3, hspace=0.35)\n","\n","ax1 = fig.add_subplot(gs[0, :])\n","ax1.plot(df['Date_only'], df['Daily_Return'], color='#e76f51', linewidth=1.8, label='Daily Return (%)')\n","ax1.plot(df['Date_only'], df['Rolling_Volatility'], color='#264653', linewidth=1.5, linestyle='--', label='30-Day Rolling Volatility (%)')\n","ax1.set_title('Daily Return Percentage of Bitcoin with Rolling Volatility', fontsize=18)\n","ax1.set_ylabel('Return (%)', fontsize=14)\n","ax1.legend(loc='upper right', fontsize=12)\n","ax1.grid(True, linestyle='--', alpha=0.5)\n","\n","# Histogram subplot (bottom left)\n","ax2 = fig.add_subplot(gs[1, 0])\n","ax2.hist(df['Daily_Return'].dropna(), bins=100, color='#264653', alpha=0.75, edgecolor='black')\n","ax2.set_title('Distribution of Daily Returns', fontsize=18)\n","ax2.set_xlabel('Daily Return (%)', fontsize=10)\n","ax2.set_ylabel('Frequency', fontsize=10)\n","ax2.grid(True, linestyle='--', alpha=0.5)\n","\n","# Boxplot subplot (bottom middle)\n","ax3 = fig.add_subplot(gs[1, 1])\n","ax3.boxplot(df['Daily_Return'].dropna(), vert=False, patch_artist=True,\n","            boxprops=dict(facecolor='#264653', color='#264653'),\n","            medianprops=dict(color='yellow'),\n","            whiskerprops=dict(color='#264653'),\n","            capprops=dict(color='#264653'),\n","            flierprops=dict(markerfacecolor='#264653', marker='o', markersize=5, linestyle='none', markeredgecolor='none'))\n","ax3.set_title('Boxplot of Daily Returns', fontsize=18)\n","ax3.set_xlabel('Daily Return (%)', fontsize=10)\n","ax3.grid(True, linestyle='--', alpha=0.5)\n","ax3.set_yticks([])\n","\n","# Stats text box (bottom right)\n","ax4 = fig.add_subplot(gs[1, 2])\n","ax4.axis('off')\n","\n","stats_text = (\n","    f\"Count: {int(stats['count'])}\\n\"\n","    f\"Mean: {stats['mean']:.4f}\\n\"\n","    f\"Std: {stats['std']:.4f}\\n\"\n","    f\"Min: {stats['min']:.4f}\\n\"\n","    f\"25%: {stats['25%']:.4f}\\n\"\n","    f\"50% (Median): {stats['50%']:.4f}\\n\"\n","    f\"75%: {stats['75%']:.4f}\\n\"\n","    f\"Max: {stats['max']:.4f}\"\n",")\n","\n","ax4.text(0, 0.5, stats_text, fontsize=14, va='center', ha='left', fontfamily='monospace')\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"02bbccde","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.144097,"end_time":"2025-10-21T10:45:44.687771","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-10-21T10:45:44.543674","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["<div style=\"border: 2px solid #264653; padding: 15px; background-color: #ffffff;line-height:25px\">\n","    \n","While the majority of daily return changes remain within a ±10% range, sporadic sharp spikes indicate episodes of extreme volatility. These bursts are often triggered by sudden market shocks, significant news events, or major announcements impacting Bitcoin’s price. Over the years, as Bitcoin’s overall price level has increased dramatically, the amplitude of these daily fluctuations has also expanded. This rising volatility means that the daily return percentage exhibits larger swings in both directions, making it more difficult to use as a straightforward target variable for prediction models. The growing scale of these movements introduces challenges in achieving consistent and reliable forecasts.\n","\n","This evolving volatility pattern underscores the need for analysts to consider alternative approaches—such as adjusted metrics, normalization methods, or volatility-aware models—to better capture Bitcoin’s complex price dynamics and improve predictive robustness."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"881363db","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.14166,"end_time":"2025-10-21T10:45:44.98792","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-10-21T10:45:44.84626","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["<a id=\"sma\"></a>\n","\n","<h1 style=\" \n","    background-color:#cddcdf; \n","    background-position: center;\n","    font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\n","    font-size: 1.5em;\n","    color: Black;\n","    text-align: center;\n","    padding: 15px;\n","    border-radius: 5px 10px;\n","\">\n","    Simple Moving Average Analysis\n","</h1>"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"6a5e6389","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.142302,"end_time":"2025-10-21T10:45:45.273395","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-10-21T10:45:45.131093","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["<div style=\"border: 2px solid #264653; padding: 15px; background-color: #ffffff;line-height:25px\">\n","    \n","**Simple Moving Average (SMA): An Essential Technical Indicator for Financial Analysis**\n","\n","The Simple Moving Average (SMA) is one of the most fundamental and widely utilized technical indicators in the realm of financial markets. It serves as a crucial analytical tool that calculates the arithmetic mean of an asset's price over a predetermined number of trading days. By averaging out price data, the SMA effectively smooths out short-term volatility and random fluctuations, allowing investors and analysts to discern underlying price trends more clearly.\n","\n","In this analysis, we compute SMAs using the closing prices over various time horizons—specifically 3-day, 7-day, 15-day, and 30-day intervals. These different windows provide insights into both short-term and medium-to-long-term market momentum, facilitating a comprehensive understanding of price dynamics.\n","\n","**Mathematically, the SMA is defined as:**\n","\n","$$\n","\\text{SMA}_n = \\frac{P_1 + P_2 + \\dots + P_n}{n}\n","$$\n","\n","Where:\n","\n","* $P_1, P_2, \\ldots, P_n$ represent the closing prices of the asset over the most recent $n$ trading days.\n","* $n$ is the length of the moving average window, corresponding to the number of days considered.\n","\n","*To maintain continuity and accuracy in the SMA series, any initial missing values—naturally occurring because of insufficient data points at the start of the time series—are thoughtfully filled with the available closing prices. This approach ensures the moving averages remain smooth and reliable from the outset.*\n","\n","By leveraging these SMAs, market participants can more effectively identify and differentiate between short-term fluctuations and enduring price trends. This enhanced visibility aids in making informed trading decisions, optimizing entry and exit points, and managing risk in an ever-changing market environment. The calculated SMAs thus serve as a cornerstone for both technical analysis and strategic financial planning. "]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":26,"id":"7b0d036e","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2025-10-21T10:45:45.559339Z","iopub.status.busy":"2025-10-21T10:45:45.55901Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-10-21T10:45:45.569749Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-10-21T10:45:45.568854Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.156033,"end_time":"2025-10-21T10:45:45.571075","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-10-21T10:45:45.415042","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["windows = [3, 7, 15, 30, 50]\n","\n","for window in windows:\n","    col_name = f'SMA{window}'\n","    df[col_name] = df['Close'].rolling(window=window).mean()\n","    df[col_name] = df[col_name].fillna(df['Close'])"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":27,"id":"09274e71","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2025-10-21T10:45:45.851876Z","iopub.status.busy":"2025-10-21T10:45:45.851569Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-10-21T10:45:46.465422Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-10-21T10:45:46.4645Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.76066,"end_time":"2025-10-21T10:45:46.472183","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-10-21T10:45:45.711523","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1500x800 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n","df['Date_o