:"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["<div style=\"border: 2px solid #264653; padding: 15px; background-color: #ffffff;line-height:25px\">\n","    \n","The 3-day Simple Moving Average (SMA3) tracks the closing price very closely because of its short calculation window, which makes it highly sensitive to daily price movements. Moving to the 7-day SMA (SMA7), it effectively reduces short-term noise while still preserving the essential characteristics of the underlying trend. Meanwhile, the 15-day (SMA15) and 30-day (SMA30) moving averages produce progressively smoother lines, reflecting medium- to longer-term market trends with less sensitivity to daily fluctuations. The 50-day SMA (SMA50) further extends this smoothing effect, offering a clear view of the long-term trend by filtering out much of the short- and medium-term volatility.\n","\n","In essence, shorter-period SMAs like SMA3 react quickly to recent price changes, providing timely signals but with more volatility. Conversely, longer-period SMAs such as SMA30 and SMA50 respond more slowly, introducing lag but delivering a more stable and reliable indication of the broader trend."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"4d5fffbd","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.153684,"end_time":"2025-10-21T10:45:49.889281","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-10-21T10:45:49.735597","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["<a id=\"ema\"></a>\n","\n","<h1 style=\" \n","    background-color:#cddcdf; \n","    background-position: center;\n","    font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\n","    font-size: 1.5em;\n","    color: Black;\n","    text-align: center;\n","    padding: 15px;\n","    border-radius: 5px 10px;\n","\">\n","    Exponential Moving Average Analysis\n","</h1>"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"5167cb3d","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.154804,"end_time":"2025-10-21T10:45:50.197486","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-10-21T10:45:50.042682","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["<div style=\"border: 2px solid #264653; padding: 15px; background-color: #ffffff;line-height:25px\">\n","    \n","**Exponential Moving Average (EMA): A Sophisticated Tool for Responsive Trend Analysis**\n","\n","The Exponential Moving Average (EMA) stands as a refined and widely embraced technical indicator within financial analytics, designed to give greater emphasis to the most recent price data. Unlike the Simple Moving Average, which treats all past prices equally, the EMA applies exponentially decreasing weights to older prices, thereby enhancing its sensitivity to the latest market shifts and enabling quicker detection of emerging trends.\n","\n","In this analysis, EMAs are computed over 15-day and 30-day periods based on closing prices, employing the parameter `adjust=False` to maintain consistent weight application throughout the dataset. This methodological choice preserves the integrity and smoothness of the trend signal.\n","\n","**Formally, the EMA is defined by the recursive relation:**\n","\n","$$\n","\\text{EMA}_t = (P_t \\times \\alpha) + \\text{EMA}_{t-1} \\times (1 - \\alpha)\n","$$\n","\n","Where:\n","\n","* $P_t$ represents the current price at time $t$ (commonly the closing price).\n","* $\\alpha$ (alpha) is the smoothing factor, calculated as $2/(n+1)$, with $n$ denoting the chosen EMA span length.\n","* $\\text{EMA}_{t-1}$ corresponds to the EMA value from the immediately preceding period.\n","\n","This formulation ensures that recent prices exert a stronger influence on the EMA, thereby making it more reactive to the latest market dynamics compared to the SMA.\n","\n","By integrating the EMA into their analytical toolkit, traders and financial professionals gain a nuanced, timely perspective on price momentum. The EMA’s heightened responsiveness facilitates more agile decision-making, enabling market participants to identify trend reversals and confirm ongoing price movements with greater precision. Ultimately, the EMA complements broader technical analysis frameworks by delivering a smoothed yet adaptive view of evolving market conditions."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":29,"id":"f086baef","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2025-10-21T10:45:50.506253Z","iopub.status.busy":"2025-10-21T10:45:50.505947Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-10-21T10:45:51.15052Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-10-21T10:45:51.149645Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.80478,"end_time":"2025-10-21T10:45:51.15586","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-10-21T10:45:50.35108","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1500x800 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n","ema_windows = [3, 7, 15, 30, 50]\n","for window in ema_windows:\n","    df[f'EMA{window}'] = df['Close'].ewm(span=window, adjust=False).mean()\n","\n","colors_sma = {\n","    'Close': '#264653',\n","    'SMA3': '#2a9d8f',\n","    'SMA7': '#f77f00',\n","    'SMA15': '#fcbf49',\n","    'SMA30': '#eae2b7',\n","    'SMA50': '#90be6d'\n","}\n","\n","colors_ema = {\n","    'EMA3': '#9e0059',\n","    'EMA7': '#7209b7',\n","    'EMA15': '#3a0ca3',\n","    'EMA30': '#4361ee',\n","    'EMA50': '#a988dd'\n","}\n","\n","fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(15, 8))\n","\n","ax.plot(df['Date_only'], df['Close'], label='Close', color=colors_sma['Close'], linewidth=2)\n","\n","for key, color in colors_sma.items():\n","    if key != 'Close':\n","        ax.plot(df['Date_only'], df[key], label=key, linestyle='--', color=color, linewidth=1.5)\n","\n","for key, color in colors_ema.items():\n","    ax.plot(df['Date_only'], df[key], label=key, linestyle=':', color=color, linewidth=1.5)\n","\n","ax.set_xlabel(\"Date\", fontsize=14)\n","ax.set_ylabel(\"Price\", fontsize=14)\n","ax.set_title(\"Comparison of Close Price, SMA, and EMA Indicators\", fontsize=18)\n","ax.legend(loc='upper left', fontsize=10)\n","ax.grid(alpha=0.4, linestyle='--')\n","\n","axin = ax.inset_axes([0.15, 0.35, 0.35, 0.35])\n","\